course: dictionary
lesson: 5884
title: Words with a story behind them
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words get their meaning from a story. In «In the desert God fed the people with manna, bread from heaven, enough for each day», the clues are «bread from heaven» and «enough for each day». So manna must be a food that came down like a gift, just enough for one day.
explain: The clues also tell you something else. «Kept overnight it went bad» means the food could not be stored. The people gathered only what they needed each day, because extra manna spoiled.
explain: Today, «manna from heaven» means a lucky help just when you need it. Check the meaning by swapping it in: «God fed the people with food from heaven» still makes sense, so the meaning fits.
fact: Manna is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some manna, not a manna.
fact: «Manna» means the special food God sent from heaven each morning to feed the Israelites in the desert, in the Bible.
fact: «Manna from heaven» means a lucky help just when you need it.
fact: In the Bible story, the people gathered only as much manna as they needed each day, because «kept overnight it went bad».
fact: «Like manna» describes something welcome and unexpected, a gift that arrives just when it is needed.
exercise: In the desert God fed the people with «manna». What is manna? | A tent used by travellers | A river in Egypt | A type of desert animal | *Bread-like food sent from heaven
exercise: What happened to manna kept overnight? | *It went bad | It was sold in the market | It flew back to heaven | It grew into a tree
exercise: Maya says, «Finding the bus fare when I'd lost my purse was manna from heaven.» What does it mean? | A bus that goes to heaven | *A lucky help just when you need it | A very heavy meal | A holiday in the desert
test: What does «like manna» suggest about something? | Heavy and slow to move | *Welcome and unexpected, like a lucky gift | Cold and wet | Dangerous and sharp
test: Which phrase means a lucky help just when you need it? | forty years | *manna from heaven | in the desert | the Promised Land
exam: The people gathered manna each day, but only as much as they needed, because «kept overnight it went bad». What lesson does this show? | *Take only what you need, because extra food spoils | Heaven sends more food when you ask for it | Food is always cheap in the desert | Store as much as you can for the future
